  "kind": "Bounded search admission design model with reviewed concrete guards; not a production refinement proof.",
  "correspondence": "One request, nine remote result classes, two fixed selection pins, four independent epoch owners and a two-tick deadline. Source hashes bind reviewed working-tree bytes; source_base is their baseline, not a claim that new bytes were already committed.",
  "review_basis": "Preserves SearchAdmission v4 transitions, complete independent expected rule inventories and expected counterexamples. Reviews REST preflight before MCP dispatch, verified same-physical-entry access, explicit connection/grant epoch checks before and after refresh, current physical page/owner/stable-claim/source admission, retained disabled observations, supporting File binding rereads, and final source/credential/deadline fences. The hosted wire decoder accepts only observed workspace_search shapes and never upgrades remote matching to exact consumption-byte proof. Broker owns disabled tool registration, host session/metadata qualification and active pins; its separate suite and installed Pi acceptance must establish those obligations. Node source-mode review: the package-version import now uses the existing default JSON import with type=json attribute and reads the same manifest.version. This corrects native Node module loading; operation, admission, deadline, credential and result semantics are unchanged. The existing real source-mode dev-launcher regression and full installed-package check must pass. Native Node type-erasure review: NotionMcpClient stores the identical options through an explicit readonly field and constructor assignment instead of a TypeScript parameter property. Transport, schema, byte/deadline budgets and result guards are unchanged; the real source-mode launcher, transport and SDK regressions verify this boundary. Reviewed the AH-1277 SDK boundary extraction at 90051b844aa15a86975054c81df83981c3c3a028 against ffe3b0255bea1d5a12a62c3832ec7f7175c27dd1. runOperation now delegates to the shared runRuntimeOperation while retaining the consumption capability check before service acquisition. The complete per-call environment, pre-abort check, nodeRuntime/ConfigProvider, Notion acquisition, Effect.scoped lifetime, AbortSignal, error propagation and final metrics callback retain their reviewed behavior. The helper is independently hash-bound below so moving the implementation does not remove its protection. Resolving cwd now precedes rejection of an invalid readOnly option; this changes no legal invocation or network admission and is outside the finite model. Management chooses its own factory; consumption still uses its existing read-only boundary. No finite model, configuration, independent rule inventory or existing guard mutation target changes. This is a source-correspondence review, not a new verification result.",
